Z||000000||82-T/A||12-08-2000||10:11 AM||||I recently started fixing up my 1984 Fiero 2m4 SE. I actually gave it to my parents as a Christmas present, but they put over 30k miles on it, and it's running a little rough now. The suspension is shot and the motor burns a little oil now.<P>I'm doing the suspension right now, and will start on the motor in a month.<P>The mods I will have are..<P>1) Sealed Power Hi-Output Camshaft from the Fiero Store.<BR>2) TRW Forged Pistons with Chrome Molybdenum pistons. <BR>3) New bearings all around.<BR>4) Hi output oil pump.<BR>5) K&N air filter (i know.. does nothing)<BR>6) Acccel Super Coil (painted black to look stock)<BR>7) Crane gold roller rockers.<BR>8) Chevy S-10 crank<BR>9) Hooker header (maybe.. not sure yet).<P>I want the car to look TOTALLY original at any glance, short of removing the valve cover.<P>I have been using Car Test, and it says I should be running high 15s.. which I don't believe. I figure it will probably be running maybe low 16s.<P>Any ideas?<P>Or if any of you have any other suggestions on what I might do or change to help improve performance or reliability in my rebuild.. I'd like to hear it.<P>Thanks!<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||5
Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-08-2000||02:28 PM||||i'd say high 15s.. Aaron Billups (Butler Tire here in atl) has a 87 4cyl with a 4 puck clutch (I installed, same as GT Bastards) Yokohama Avid H4s on the stock 15" lace GT wheels. and no air filter will run 15.4... it's got about 70k on it. thats a nice laundy list of go fast goodies! there a dyno near you? Dyno it now and then after the new motor is in!  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||12-08-2000||05:37 PM||||Give me your camshaft specifications, transmission type, and the cars weight with you in it and I can give you some simulations from Dyno2000 and Dragstrip2000.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||12-08-2000||06:50 PM||||Well since your 85 GT ran 14s, I think you could easily break 13s with a built up Fiero at that track...<P>hehe <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||82-T/A||12-08-2000||09:10 PM||||Black88GT, correction, HIGH 14s.<P>But either way, my point really isn't to hot rod the car, I just want to be able to pass UPS trucks and stuff. <P>I'm shooting for low 16s. I'd be fine with that. I just want it to be "quick" in the TRUE sense of the word, and handle like it did when it was new.. and still be reliable.<P>Thanks Formula, I'll get the specs on it.<P><P>------------------<BR>Todd Jaspers<BR>1997 Pontiac GrandAm SE<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero SE/V6<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2m4 SE<BR>http://www.ezshots.com/album.cgi?82tafiero/Apartment||||reg||1
